---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Mutual Respect" description="We support lawful immigration enforcement. We ask that it treat foreign guests with the respect we hope Americans receive abroad.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="zh-title" lang="zh-Hant">相互尊重</p>
      <h1>Enforce the law. Respect the guest.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        We support the mission of immigration enforcement. A country has every right to decide who enters and
        stays. We also believe how that power is used matters, and that the respect we show visitors here is
        the respect Americans can expect when they travel, study and work abroad.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">The principle</p>
      <h2>Treat guests the way we want to be treated.</h2>
      <p>
        Every year Americans study abroad, attend conferences, do business and visit family overseas. When one
        of them is stopped at a border, we expect them to be told why, to be able to call their consulate and a
        lawyer, to be treated with dignity, and to be released quickly if there is no real cause to hold them.
        We ask nothing more for the students, scholars and visitors who come here.
      </p>
      <p>
        That reciprocity is not a favor. It is what makes it possible for people to cross borders to learn from
        one another at all. Mutual respect is the basis for collaboration.
      </p>
      <blockquote>
        Supporting enforcement and asking it to do better are not opposites. Good enforcement earns public trust;
        careless enforcement spends it.
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">What better enforcement looks like</p>
      <h2>Six reasonable standards</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-3">
        <div class="card accent">
          <h3>Judgment first</h3>
          <p class="muted">Use discretion. Students and researchers in valid visa status who travel for their work and come back to continue it should not be the priority for detention.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card accent">
          <h3>Say why</h3>
          <p class="muted">Tell people clearly, in a language they understand, why they are being stopped or held and what happens next.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card accent">
          <h3>Counsel and consulate</h3>
          <p class="muted">Prompt access to a lawyer and to consular officials, as the Vienna Convention on Consular Relations provides and as we expect for Americans held abroad.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card accent">
          <h3>Dignity in custody</h3>
          <p class="muted">Humane conditions, respectful conduct and no unnecessary force, for every person, whatever their status.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card accent">
          <h3>Detention as a last resort</h3>
          <p class="muted">Use alternatives to detention when someone has deep community ties and poses no danger, and keep any detention as short as possible.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card accent">
          <h3>Talk to institutions</h3>
          <p class="muted">When a student or scholar is held, notify and work with their university, so questions can be answered quickly instead of by detention.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="brief">
    <div class="wrap brief">
      <a class="brief-thumb" href="/downloads/free-eva-congress-brief.pdf">
        <img src="/downloads/thumbs/congress-brief.webp" alt="One page policy brief: Enforce the law. Respect the guest." width="320" height="414" loading="lazy" />
      </a>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">For lawmakers and staff</p>
        <h2>The one page brief</h2>
        <p>
          A single page for members of Congress and their staff: Eva&#8217;s situation, why this is common ground for
          both parties, the six standards above, and three practical asks. Prepared for the bipartisan Problem Solvers
          Caucus. Print it on US Letter paper; the QR code links to the petition.
        </p>
        <div class="btn-row">
          <a class="btn" href="/downloads/free-eva-congress-brief.pdf" download>Download the brief (PDF)</a>
          <a class="btn ghost" href="/downloads/free-eva-congress-brief.png" download>Image (PNG)</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Take action</p>
      <h2>How to move this forward</h2>
      <ol class="actions">
        <li>
          <h3>Write to Congress about standards</h3>
          <p>Ask your representative and senators to support clear, published guidance on how ICE and CBP handle students and scholars in valid visa status, including access to counsel and timely notice to universities.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Ask your university to have a plan</h3>
          <p>Ask your school's international office what it does when a student is detained while traveling, and whether it offers advice before travel and legal contacts.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Keep it respectful</h3>
          <p>Officers carry out policy; policy is set by elected officials and agency leaders. Direct pressure there, and treat everyone, including officers, with the respect we are asking for.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Tell the reciprocity story</h3>
          <p>If you have been a guest in another country, a student, scholar or traveler, share how you were treated and how you would want to be treated. Personal stories move people.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .brief { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(180px, 300px) 1fr; gap: 2.5rem; align-items: center; }
  .brief-thumb { display: block; border-radius: 6px; overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid var(--line); box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.45); transition: transform 0.15s; }
  .brief-thumb:hover { transform: translateY(-3px); }
  .brief-thumb img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { .brief { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; } .brief-thumb { max-width: 260px; } }
</style>
